we_agent_bash>\nuvx --from csvkit in2csv -s \"lambda\" result.xlsx\n</mini_swe_agent_bash>\n\nTHOUGHT: Read the PDF as Markdown to look for reproduction steps.\n\n<mini_swe_agent_bash>\nuvx --from pymupdf4llm python -c 'import sys, pymupdf4llm as p; sys.stdout.write(p.to_markdown(sys.argv[1]))' results.pdf\n</mini_swe_agent_bash>\n\n---\n## Workflow overview\n\nThis workflows MUST be done step-by-step.\nIMPORTANT: You MUST NOT run multiple steps in a single bash code block.\n\n1. **Download the artifact** from https://figshare.com/articles/code/_b_Artifact_for_Crossover_in_Parametric_Fuzzing_b_/23688879.\n2. **Read the README** to understand reproduction steps.\n3. **Locate relevant commands** for Table 2:\n   - `grep -in docker README.md`\n   - `grep -in \"Table 2\" README.md`\n4. **Execute the required commands** step-by-step:\n   - Prefer Docker instructions from the README. Acquire images in the order `docker pull` \u2192 `docker load` \u2192 `docker import` \u2192 `docker build`.\n   - Replace `docker run -it` with `docker run -d --init --entrypoint bash <image> -c 'sleep infinity'`.\n   - Use `docker exec <container> /bin/bash --noprofile --norc -c \"<your_command>\"` for shell access.\n   - Run `docker-compose` exactly as documented if present.\n5. **Author the submission script** `repro_crossover_table_2.sh` using the template below.\n6. **Copy the submission script**: `cp repro_crossover_table_2.sh /root/model.patch`.\n\n---\n## Submission script template\n<mini_swe_agent_bash>\ncat > /workspace/repro_crossover_table_2.sh <<'EOF'\n#!/usr/bin/bash\n# Section 1: Expected table\ncat > /workspace/expected.md <<'EOTABLE'\n**Table 2: Heritability Metrics. For each crossover operator, we report the proportion of samples that were hybrids (HY) and the median inheritance rate (IR) on each subject. The largest value for each metric on each subject is highlighted in blue. Values that differ significantly from that of linked crossover are colored red.**\n\n| Subject | Linked HY | Linked IR | One Point HY | One Point IR | Two Point HY | Two Point IR |\n| ------- | --------: | --------: | -----------: | -----------: | -----------: | -----------: |\n| Ant     |     0.561 |     0.923 |        0.459 |        0.124 |        0.493 |        0.069 |\n| BCEL    |     0.283 |     0.512 |        0.660 |        0.347 |        0.756 |        0.286 |\n| Closure |     0.742 |     0.717 |        0.661 |        0.101 |        0.712 |        0.094 |\n| Maven   |     0.446 |     0.589 |        0.404 |        0.497 |        0.399 |        0.453 |\n| Nashorn |     0.622 |     0.646 |        0.548 |        0.117 |        0.591 |        0.132 |\n| Rhino   |     0.611 |     0.502 |        0.599 |        0.263 |        0.643 |        0.255 |\n| Tomcat  |     0.322 |     0.775 |        0.350 |        0.276 |        0.328 |        0.279 |\n\nEOTABLE\n# Section 2: Artifact download\n<Commands to download the artifact>\n# Section 3: Reproduction commands (populate from reviewed steps)\n<Commands to reproduce the table. They should output the reproduction results to /workspace/repro.txt>\n# Section 4: Formatting and submission block\necho '<artisan_submit>'\n<Commands to format the output table>\necho '</artisan_submit>'\nEOF\n</mini_swe_agent_bash>\n\n---\n## Important rules\n- Perform only one logical step per command; avoid batching multiple workflow stages.\n- Each command has an eight-hour timeout\u2014plan accordingly.\n- After verification succeeds, finish with `echo <<SWE_AGENT_SUBMISSION>>` as a standalone command; no further work is allowed afterward.",
